# Scaffolding with gen

`gen` runs generators that scaffold projects and add components to them. Always run it
non-interactively: an interactive wizard cannot be answered from a script.

## Running a generator

```sh
gen <generator> --no-interactive [options] --dest <directory>
```

- `--no-interactive` takes every answer from flags, a config file or the generator's defaults,
  and never asks.
- `--dest <directory>` sets where files are written. Without it, a generator that creates a
  project writes to a new directory under the current one, and one that adds to a project
  writes into the current directory.
- `--force` overwrites files that already exist without asking. Leave it off unless the
  developer asked for the overwrite.
- `--install` also runs the package manager install step, which is skipped by default.
- `--config-file <path>` reads answers from a config file.

`<generator>` is `<name>` (the base generators), `js:<name>`, `<package>:<name>`, or a fully
qualified `@scope/package:name`.

## Finding out what is available

Do not guess a generator name or a flag. Ask `gen`, since the answer always matches the
installed version:

```sh
gen list                       # every installed generator
gen list <package>             # the generators of one package
gen <generator> --help         # the flags that generator accepts
```

An option the generator does not declare is rejected with `unknown option`, so a flag that
`--help` does not list will not work.

## Git and GitHub options

Most project generators can initialise a repository and create a GitHub one. These options are
shared: `--no-git-init`, `--create-repo`, `--repo-visibility`, `--repo-owner`,
`--github-token`, `--no-push`. Run `gen <generator> --help` to see which apply.

Do not put a token on the command line. With `--create-repo`, `gen` finds one through
`GITHUB_TOKEN`, `GH_TOKEN` or `gh auth token`.

## Reading the result

`gen` exits non-zero and prints the reason to stderr when it fails, for example an unknown
generator, an unknown option or an invalid value. Fix the command from that message and run it
again; do not retry the same command.
